Optimize both databases to avoid unnecessary reads and writes.

Read Optimization

- No page request before that page is opened.
- No full-table reads.
- Use indexed queries.
- Use pagination.
- Use cache-first loading.
- Avoid repeated identical queries.
- Deduplicate concurrent requests.
- Request only required columns where supported.
- Use batch reads only when justified.
- Avoid repeated polling.
- Avoid unnecessary background refreshes.

Write Optimization

- Do not write unchanged records.
- Compare existing and incoming values.
- Update only changed fields where supported.
- Use batch writes where supported.
- Avoid unnecessary timestamp updates.
- Avoid duplicate installation tracking writes.
- Avoid duplicate source records.
- Use idempotent operations.
- Use bounded retries with backoff.
- Prevent concurrent duplicate writes.
- Avoid continuous synchronization loops.

